    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **45 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors** \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nFollowing the existing pattern in this codebase (the `identityKey` derived field is a `@Transient` getter on `Owner` that MapStruct auto-maps to the DTO), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer, 0\u20139) to the `Owner` response schema, right after `customerCode`. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `checkDigit` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` method implementing the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits in `customerCode` (non-digit characters like the `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-` prefix and separators are skipped; a null code is treated as no digits). MapStruct auto-maps this getter to the DTO's `checkDigit` field, so no explicit mapping was needed.\n\nThe algorithm matches the reference `luhn(...)` the acceptance test (`Cp31Tests`) uses to recompute and assert the exact digit. Nothing else regressed.",
